  "description": "A free, open-source (MIT) C# PDF library for .NET — generate PDF documents\n       (invoices, reports, receipts, labels, certificates) from code with a fluent,\n       composable API. Lightweight, zero-dependency, and pure managed C#: no native\n       binaries, no HTML-to-PDF browser engine, free for commercial use. Features\n       include rich text styling (bold, italic, underline, strikethrough, custom\n       line-height), multi-span mixed formatting, Column / Row / Table layouts,\n       PNG and JPEG image embedding, rounded and per-edge borders, explicit page\n       breaks, clickable hyperlink annotations, headers, footers, page numbers,\n       AES-256 encryption, Code128 barcodes, QR codes (ISO/IEC 18004), and a full\n       Material Design colour palette. Runs on Windows, Linux, macOS, Docker,\n       Azure, and AWS on .NET 8, 9, and 10.",
